WEBVTT

00:00.432 --> 00:03.663
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.933 --> 00:07.035
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.069 --> 00:10.739
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.773 --> 00:13.742
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.776 --> 00:17.145
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.180 --> 00:20.415
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.449 --> 00:21.917
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:21.951 --> 00:23.485
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.519 --> 00:23.900
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.165 --> 00:35.944
It's that time of year again.

00:36.068 --> 00:38.425
Are you a New England dirtbag
who wants to run with bulls,

00:38.449 --> 00:40.097
but thinks Spain is gay?

00:40.585 --> 00:42.861
Then don't miss
the Seriously Wicked Bull Run

00:42.885 --> 00:44.444
in South Attleboro, Mass!

00:44.468 --> 00:47.171
You and your friends can run
from a bunch live bulls,

00:47.172 --> 00:49.778
and lots of times, there's a
chick whose boob comes out.

00:49.978 --> 00:51.739
Order your tickets
before it too late!

00:55.053 --> 00:56.137
Toilets limited.

00:56.161 --> 00:57.910
Wow, that seems
pretty cool.

00:57.934 --> 01:00.140
Nah, I don't know.
Seems pretty lame to me.

01:00.164 --> 01:01.537
Yeah, waste of time.

01:01.561 --> 01:02.304
I agree.

01:02.318 --> 01:03.592
Hey Joe,
isn't this your round?

01:03.616 --> 01:05.130
Sure.
I'll wheel over to the bar

01:05.154 --> 01:06.166
and bring back your beers

01:06.190 --> 01:07.673
one by one in my lap.

01:08.520 --> 01:10.498
You guys, we are
so doing that bull run.

01:10.598 --> 01:12.245
Buying the tickets as we speak!

01:12.269 --> 01:13.163
But we can't tell Joe.

01:13.187 --> 01:14.847
Of course not,
he'll  be dead weight.

01:14.848 --> 01:16.882
You can't do a bull run
with a guy in a wheelchair.

01:16.917 --> 01:19.351
Yeah, this is for athletes.

01:24.725 --> 01:27.025
Just the regular wash, please.

01:27.060 --> 01:30.061
And, uh, I'm supposed to mention
that I saw you on LivingSocial?

01:30.097 --> 01:31.263
Was that worth it?

01:31.298 --> 01:33.298
Was that worth the
one dollar you saved?

01:33.333 --> 01:35.734
I'm sorry, we're not doing
that promotion anymore.

01:35.769 --> 01:36.835
Oh-ho!

01:36.870 --> 01:40.205
All the humiliation,
none of the reward.

01:43.343 --> 01:46.645
You know, some people are okay
with the drive-through car wash.

01:46.680 --> 01:49.047
Me, I'm a fan of the hand job.

01:49.082 --> 01:50.215
Hi, I'm Brian.

01:50.250 --> 01:51.883
Yes, I like to have fun
with language.

01:51.919 --> 01:53.885
You're so funny.

01:53.921 --> 01:55.153
I'm Tori.

01:55.189 --> 01:56.555
I got hit by a car
in high school,

01:56.590 --> 01:57.956
so I don't have to work.

01:57.991 --> 02:00.225
Cool. Hey, so what's
your afternoon like?

02:00.260 --> 02:01.526
I don't have plans.

02:01.562 --> 02:04.296
Maybe we could grab lunch
and then see what happens.

02:04.331 --> 02:06.431
This will not end well.

02:06.466 --> 02:08.466
Like eating an artichoke.

02:08.502 --> 02:09.835
Good Lord!

02:09.870 --> 02:12.971
I ate nothing and I'm
soaking wet for some reason.

02:16.643 --> 02:18.577
So, you guys all pumped
to run with the bulls?

02:18.612 --> 02:20.579
You bet, this is gonna be
my first exercise

02:20.614 --> 02:22.581
since I chased that balloon.

02:22.616 --> 02:23.815
Hey, what's going on?

02:23.851 --> 02:24.950
Hey, Joe.

02:24.985 --> 02:27.085
We are competing...

02:27.120 --> 02:30.655
in the international Chef
Boyardee look-alike contest.

02:30.691 --> 02:32.657
Oh, well,
where's your chef hat?

02:32.693 --> 02:34.025
You guys are gonna lose.

02:34.061 --> 02:35.460
Especially Cleveland.

02:35.495 --> 02:36.928
He's in the Cream of Wheat
competition,

02:36.964 --> 02:38.396
which is down the street.

02:38.432 --> 02:39.965
We-we got to go now.
We're very late.

02:40.000 --> 02:42.300
Well, this is funny, because...

02:42.336 --> 02:43.969
guess where I'm going.

02:44.004 --> 02:45.437
And I got the hat.

02:45.472 --> 02:46.805
You guys are dead!

02:46.840 --> 02:48.840
Look, Joe.

02:48.876 --> 02:50.742
We didn't want to tell
you, but we're going

02:50.777 --> 02:52.410
to the Seriously
Wicked Bull Run.

02:52.446 --> 02:55.280
We didn't invite you because we
didn't think you could keep up.

02:55.315 --> 02:58.149
Yeah, we thought it seemed
too dangerous for, uh,

02:58.185 --> 03:01.786
incapacitated, half-man,
shrivel-legged gimps.

03:01.822 --> 03:03.655
And we didn't want
to hurt your feelings.

03:03.690 --> 03:06.057
Come on, my handicap
has never held me back.

03:06.093 --> 03:07.626
I'm coming with you guys.

03:07.661 --> 03:10.095
Joe, you peed in your bag
while you said that.

03:10.130 --> 03:12.297
Can you honestly say
that you didn't pee

03:12.332 --> 03:15.133
just now while you
were talking?

03:15.168 --> 03:17.335
Okay, you can come.

03:21.375 --> 03:24.075
Wow, that was amazing.

03:24.111 --> 03:25.243
Hey, uh, uh,
just to be clear,

03:25.279 --> 03:26.845
I don't really
think you're a whore.

03:26.880 --> 03:29.981
I-I just need to say that
to, you know, to finish.

03:30.017 --> 03:31.983
Oh, yeah, yeah,
yeah, of course.

03:32.019 --> 03:34.219
And obviously, I don't think
you're my Uncle Dale.

03:34.254 --> 03:35.420
Good, good, same page.

03:36.623 --> 03:38.490
Oh, crap,
my husband's home early.

03:38.525 --> 03:39.758
Wait a minute,
you're married?!

03:39.793 --> 03:40.959
And he's here?
Now?!

03:42.062 --> 03:43.094
Yeah, that's him.

03:43.130 --> 03:44.429
You've got to get out of here.

03:44.464 --> 03:45.830
He's really jealous.

03:45.866 --> 03:47.565
I think he's bitter
because he never got

03:47.601 --> 03:50.368
the credit he deserved
for killing Osama bin Laden.

03:50.404 --> 03:52.203
Your husband's a Navy SEAL?!

03:54.374 --> 03:55.707
What the hell
is going on here?!

03:55.742 --> 03:57.075
What is this?

03:58.879 --> 04:00.578
Ruff!

04:00.614 --> 04:02.547
You got a dog?

04:02.582 --> 04:03.949
Uh... yeah!

04:03.984 --> 04:06.217
I rescued him
from the pound.

04:08.055 --> 04:09.821
Well, hey there, buddy.

04:09.856 --> 04:11.589
Wow, his nose is super wet!

04:11.625 --> 04:13.058
He must be healthy.

04:13.093 --> 04:15.994
Uh, and somebody's been
rooting in a sardine can.

04:16.029 --> 04:18.063
Well, I'm gonna
grab a shower.

04:18.098 --> 04:20.131
Great, honey.

04:20.167 --> 04:22.100
Oh. Oh, my God,
that was close.

04:22.135 --> 04:24.035
Yeah, but think about it.

04:24.071 --> 04:26.037
As long as he thinks
you're our new pet,

04:26.073 --> 04:28.239
we can keep fooling
around behind his back.

04:28.275 --> 04:30.375
Huh, you're right.

04:30.410 --> 04:32.077
Wow, this could be
an even better scam

04:32.112 --> 04:34.612
than that claw machine
at the arcade.

04:35.816 --> 04:37.515
Damn it, this game is so stupid!

04:37.551 --> 04:40.885
It's impossible to do anything
with a dumb, crappy claw!

04:40.921 --> 04:43.221
Hey, that's mean,
and it's not even true!

04:43.256 --> 04:45.056
I'm leaving!

04:45.092 --> 04:47.092
Dang it!

04:51.031 --> 04:52.230
You need a little help?

04:52.265 --> 04:54.265
No!

04:56.403 --> 04:59.270
If you could angle up the ring,
then I could kind of hook it.

05:03.443 --> 05:04.843
How do you drive?

05:04.878 --> 05:06.644
Bad!

05:17.691 --> 05:19.424
We clearly overdressed.

05:19.459 --> 05:21.493
They have the type
of fat white woman here

05:21.528 --> 05:24.162
that not even
I am interested in.

05:24.197 --> 05:25.296
Ladies, gentlemen,

05:25.332 --> 05:27.132
and alternative high school
graduates,

05:27.167 --> 05:29.434
get ready to run for your lives!

05:37.144 --> 05:39.310
Aah! I shouldn't
have worn high heels!

05:39.346 --> 05:40.779
Oh, stop it!
You look great.

05:40.814 --> 05:43.681
<i>Oh, well, I didn't
want all this attention.</i>

05:45.218 --> 05:46.351
<i>Cleveland, why do you let them</i>

05:46.386 --> 05:47.919
<i>talk you into these things?</i>

05:47.954 --> 05:50.522
<i>This is how
people pleasers die!</i>

05:50.557 --> 05:52.357
Hey, guys, after this,
let's beat alligators

05:52.392 --> 05:53.491
with sticks or something.

05:53.527 --> 05:54.893
You read my mind!

05:54.928 --> 05:57.162
<i>We just talked about this!</i>

05:58.765 --> 06:00.565
This is amazing!

06:00.600 --> 06:02.700
I told you guys I could do it!

06:21.254 --> 06:24.856
Look... out...

06:24.891 --> 06:28.259
Joe...!

07:07.901 --> 07:10.034
Joe, oh, my God!

07:10.070 --> 07:11.469
Are you all right?!

07:11.505 --> 07:14.005
I can't feel anything
below my neck!

07:14.040 --> 07:16.241
I can't move a muscle, guys!

07:16.276 --> 07:17.408
Oh, my God!

07:17.444 --> 07:19.911
Joe's completely
paralyzed!

07:21.815 --> 07:22.847
Oop, that's me.

07:22.883 --> 07:24.082
That's unfortunate.

07:24.117 --> 07:25.483
That's Lois, hold on.

07:25.519 --> 07:26.718
Hey, babe.

07:26.753 --> 07:27.785
Uh, good.

07:27.821 --> 07:28.987
Little hiccup, but fun.

07:37.093 --> 07:39.093
You guys!

07:39.128 --> 07:41.528
I've been trying to keep
my birthday a secret.

07:41.564 --> 07:43.831
No, Dr. Hartman, we're not
here for your birthday.

07:43.866 --> 07:44.999
We're here for Joe.

07:45.034 --> 07:46.200
Don't sugarcoat it, Doc.

07:46.235 --> 07:47.668
Just give it to me straight.

07:47.703 --> 07:49.903
Well, Mr. Swanson, I did
an exploratory procedure,

07:49.939 --> 07:52.072
which revealed extensive damage.

07:52.108 --> 07:55.209
Please, just tell me--
am I completely paralyzed?

07:55.244 --> 07:56.310
I'm afraid...

07:56.345 --> 07:57.811
of ghosts.

07:57.847 --> 07:59.013
And yes.

07:59.048 --> 08:00.314
Mr. Swanson
has lost all movement,

08:00.349 --> 08:02.383
and will require
around-the-clock care.

08:02.418 --> 08:04.218
Most of it disgusting.

08:04.253 --> 08:06.687
Oh, my God, Bonnie,
I'm so sorry.

08:06.722 --> 08:08.322
If there's anything
I can do...

08:08.357 --> 08:09.723
There actually is.

08:09.759 --> 08:11.825
Could you collect
my mail forever?

08:11.861 --> 08:13.961
I'm leaving Joe
and moving to Europe.

08:13.996 --> 08:16.063
I didn't sign up for this.

08:16.098 --> 08:18.165
Bonnie, wait!
God, this is awful.

08:18.200 --> 08:20.034
What am I gonna do?

08:20.069 --> 08:22.202
Well, seems like you folks
have this all taken care of.

08:23.272 --> 08:24.238
Surprise!

08:24.273 --> 08:26.473
Oh, you guys!

08:26.509 --> 08:27.975
Hey, don't go in
that room back there.

08:28.010 --> 08:30.177
It's, like,
super sad.

08:35.384 --> 08:38.185
Coming up, quintuplets
born at Quahog General.

08:38.220 --> 08:40.087
What?
That's...

08:40.122 --> 08:41.655
Oh, that's supposed
to be "burn"?

08:41.691 --> 08:45.626
Oh, coming up, quintuplets
burn at Quahog General.

08:46.729 --> 08:49.396
Hey, honey, get in here.

08:49.432 --> 08:51.765
Check this out--
the way he's sitting,

08:51.801 --> 08:54.001
it looks like the dog's
watching the news.

08:54.036 --> 08:56.637
You like watching the
news, you dumb dog?

08:56.672 --> 08:59.606
Well, I'm off to do what
former Navy SEALs do--

08:59.642 --> 09:02.142
sell lawnmowers.

09:02.178 --> 09:04.144
Wow, he really
has no idea.

09:04.180 --> 09:06.447
Hey, want to take
a shower with me?

09:06.482 --> 09:08.082
Sure.

09:08.117 --> 09:09.650
Man, this is a pretty sweet gig.

09:09.685 --> 09:11.985
Like being a member
of Daft Punk.

09:12.021 --> 09:14.188
Look at this old Casio keyboard

09:14.223 --> 09:16.423
from the 1980s
that I have found.

09:16.459 --> 09:19.026
Watch what happens
when I push this demo button.

09:19.061 --> 09:22.429
♪ ♪

09:22.465 --> 09:23.997
Hello, Daft Punk?

09:24.033 --> 09:26.133
Great song.
Here's a Grammy.

09:26.168 --> 09:27.568
Oh-ho-ho!

09:27.603 --> 09:28.802
You know, is funny.

09:28.838 --> 09:31.772
Until you spoke, I did
not know we were French!

09:35.311 --> 09:37.578
There you go, Joe.
All settled.

09:37.613 --> 09:39.446
Now, which wall
would you like to look at

09:39.482 --> 09:40.581
for the rest of your life?

09:40.616 --> 09:42.883
I don't know,
maybe that one.

09:42.918 --> 09:44.952
I-I have no idea
what you're pointing at, Joe.

09:44.987 --> 09:46.253
You got to meet us halfway.

09:46.288 --> 09:48.222
Look, guys, I don't want
to be a burden to anyone.

09:48.257 --> 09:50.157
You go ahead
and live your lives.

09:50.192 --> 09:51.592
I'll be fine.

09:51.627 --> 09:53.227
We can't just
leave you, Joe.

09:53.262 --> 09:56.029
So before we go, I'm gonna
put the remote in your mouth.

09:56.065 --> 09:58.132
Here's a can of chili.

09:58.167 --> 10:01.335
And the opener we'll put...
in your mouth.

10:01.370 --> 10:03.303
And here's a magazine I thought
you might like to read.

10:03.339 --> 10:06.240
I'm gonna put it
in your mouth.

10:06.275 --> 10:08.208
You're a good friend, Peter.

10:08.244 --> 10:10.043
Joe, I just wish
we could do more,

10:10.079 --> 10:12.579
but obviously your
mouth is full.

10:12.615 --> 10:14.448
And you probably don't want
any reminders of Bonnie

10:14.483 --> 10:17.017
around the house, so I cleared
out all of her underwear.

10:17.052 --> 10:18.786
Okay, don't be a stranger.

10:18.821 --> 10:21.021
Yeah, 'cause we're not
supposed to talk to those.

10:21.056 --> 10:24.224
I don't know, I'm not sure
I feel right about leaving Joe.

10:24.260 --> 10:27.361
Doesn't seem like he's gonna be
able to take care of himself.

10:27.396 --> 10:29.363
Yeah, we're-we're kind
of all he has now.

10:29.398 --> 10:30.430
What-- Joe?

10:30.466 --> 10:31.532
What're you talking about?

10:31.567 --> 10:33.934
He's fine.

10:33.969 --> 10:36.537
<i>Look, he's already watching
The Price Is Right in there.</i>

10:36.572 --> 10:38.939
Oop, he's biting
too hard on the volume.

10:43.779 --> 10:45.612
Okay, you can play over there
in the sandbox, honey.

10:45.648 --> 10:47.848
Mommy's just gonna
read her book.

10:47.883 --> 10:49.783
Okay, I'm just gonna
walk 30 feet away,

10:49.819 --> 10:52.319
and then panic
because I can't see you.

10:52.354 --> 10:54.254
Can you fit me in
at 10:00 tomorrow?

10:54.290 --> 10:56.023
It's getting a little
long on the sides.

10:56.058 --> 10:58.158
Brian? What are you
doing on a leash?

10:58.194 --> 10:59.526
And who's that?

10:59.562 --> 11:00.727
Be cool.

11:00.763 --> 11:02.095
This is the guy whose
wife I'm banging.

11:02.131 --> 11:03.897
Oh, what a romantic way
to put it.

11:03.933 --> 11:05.098
Yeah, it's great.

11:05.134 --> 11:06.533
I just pretend
to be their dog,

11:06.569 --> 11:08.068
and then when he
leaves for work,

11:08.103 --> 11:11.538
<i>I get to go to the pound,
if you know what I mean.</i>

11:11.574 --> 11:13.173
God, Brian,
you are such a scumbag.

11:13.209 --> 11:14.575
I can't believe you--

11:14.610 --> 11:16.610
Mommy! Mommy!
Where's my Mommy?!

11:16.645 --> 11:18.378
I have no one and nothing!

11:18.414 --> 11:19.880
I'm right here, honey.

11:19.915 --> 11:21.248
Oh, thank God.

11:21.283 --> 11:24.017
She's such a gross hog.

11:27.823 --> 11:29.723
Joe, you can't
just sit here.

11:29.758 --> 11:31.491
You need intellectual
stimulation.

11:31.527 --> 11:33.493
So I brought something
to read to you.

11:33.529 --> 11:36.396
It's the word search
from the Sunday Circular.

11:36.432 --> 11:37.898
"Kangaroo."

11:37.933 --> 11:40.334
Let's see if we
can find that one.

11:40.369 --> 11:41.602
"Outback."

11:41.637 --> 11:43.470
I think it's an
Australian theme.

11:43.505 --> 11:44.771
"Koala."

11:44.807 --> 11:46.306
It definitely is.

11:46.342 --> 11:47.875
Can't make out this one.

11:47.910 --> 11:50.110
"Abor... Aborgine...

11:50.145 --> 11:51.645
Aborgina"?

11:51.680 --> 11:53.714
That's what they call
eggplant down there.

11:53.749 --> 11:55.349
You know what?
Forget this.

11:55.384 --> 11:57.517
<i>I'll just read
to you from Jet.</i>

11:57.553 --> 11:59.753
Look, this whole page is
all the Wayans brothers

11:59.788 --> 12:01.755
sitting in different
positions.

12:01.790 --> 12:04.358
How you suppose they come up
with all them positions?

12:04.393 --> 12:05.926
You could give me
a million years.

12:05.961 --> 12:07.928
I just ain't
wired that way.

12:07.963 --> 12:09.229
Marlon's like
a rubber man.

12:09.265 --> 12:10.831
He can sit in
any kind of way.

12:10.866 --> 12:13.634
Here's Keenan telling the
younger ones how to sit.

12:13.669 --> 12:14.968
Like they
gonna listen.

12:15.004 --> 12:16.470
Damon's doing
his own thing.

12:16.505 --> 12:17.638
No surprise there.

12:17.673 --> 12:18.839
That's Damon.

12:18.874 --> 12:20.374
You enjoying
all this, Joe?

12:20.409 --> 12:22.175
I'm honestly
just glad it seems

12:22.211 --> 12:24.311
like you have
something you like.

12:29.518 --> 12:30.918
Hey, my laptop's
out of battery.

12:30.953 --> 12:32.286
You want to have sex?

12:32.321 --> 12:35.188
Sure, I've almost finished
my sandwich, anyway.

12:36.792 --> 12:39.426
Oh, come on, I don't want
to have to watch this.

12:39.461 --> 12:40.994
Yeah, that's right.

12:41.030 --> 12:44.231
I was the only one
who didn't get to meet Biden.

12:44.266 --> 12:45.532
You know what?

12:45.567 --> 12:47.834
Screw this.
I'm out of here.

12:50.639 --> 12:53.507
Ha! Skewered.

12:53.542 --> 12:55.142
Hey!

12:55.177 --> 12:56.343
Where do you think you're going?

12:56.378 --> 12:57.444
You're my dog.

12:57.479 --> 12:59.212
You're not going anywhere.

12:59.248 --> 13:00.480
Besides, I need you, boy.

13:00.516 --> 13:02.282
Now more than ever.

13:02.318 --> 13:04.785
I think my wife
is cheating on me.

13:05.554 --> 13:07.587
Hey, Tori, it's Brian.

13:07.623 --> 13:09.222
I'm getting
the Chinese food for us.

13:09.258 --> 13:11.792
I think I'm gonna order
some Me Like Bang Ho.

13:11.827 --> 13:14.161
That's-that's not a real thing,

13:14.196 --> 13:15.629
I'm talking about sex.

13:15.664 --> 13:17.731
All right,
I'll be there in five.

13:17.766 --> 13:19.733
Man, when I find
that son of a bitch,

13:19.768 --> 13:22.069
I'm gonna rip
his head off.

13:23.706 --> 13:25.172
God, what a nightmare.

13:25.207 --> 13:28.208
That guy's even scarier
than a thesaurus-asaurus.

13:28.243 --> 13:30.944
Tread, stomp, trudge.

13:30.980 --> 13:33.447
Growl, roar, ululate.

13:33.482 --> 13:35.816
Antonym-- whisper.

13:35.851 --> 13:36.984
What's wrong with him?

13:37.019 --> 13:38.019
He's on the spectrum.

13:38.053 --> 13:39.152
"Spectrum"?

13:39.188 --> 13:40.520
In my day we'd
throw him in the army

13:40.556 --> 13:42.522
and have him
play the bugle.

13:46.195 --> 13:48.362
Peter, this just isn't working.

13:48.397 --> 13:50.263
We can't take
proper care of Joe.

13:50.299 --> 13:51.732
It's a huge amount of work

13:51.767 --> 13:52.866
and we don't have
any idea what we're doing.

13:52.901 --> 13:54.034
Quagmire's right.

13:54.069 --> 13:55.235
It's too much.

13:55.270 --> 13:56.570
I just think he'd
be better off

13:56.605 --> 13:59.539
under the care of grumpy,
Filipino nurses.

13:59.575 --> 14:01.274
Yeah, that's why
I looked into it,

14:01.310 --> 14:02.743
and we've reserved
a place for him

14:02.778 --> 14:05.445
at the State Home for
Mentals and Bastards.

14:05.481 --> 14:09.316
Oh, my God, sometimes
they whip them with hoses...

14:09.351 --> 14:11.952
outside?!
This is perfect!

14:19.795 --> 14:22.329
Hi, I work here.

14:22.364 --> 14:24.731
I don't think
this guy works here.

14:24.767 --> 14:25.866
Hi, can I help you?

14:25.901 --> 14:27.567
Yeah, this is Joe Swanson.

14:27.603 --> 14:29.936
We arranged for a 9:15 dump-off?

14:29.972 --> 14:31.505
Go on, guys, get out of here.

14:31.540 --> 14:33.073
I'll be fine.

14:33.108 --> 14:34.108
Bye, Joe.

14:34.143 --> 14:35.108
Take care, man.

14:35.144 --> 14:37.144
See ya, Joe.

14:38.647 --> 14:40.313
Hold on, guys.

14:40.349 --> 14:43.450
There's one last thing
I got to say to my friend.

14:43.485 --> 14:46.086
Hey, Joe, you know
that movie you told me to watch

14:46.121 --> 14:48.188
that you said was
your favorite movie of all time,

14:48.223 --> 14:49.322
and you said
I had to watch it?

14:49.358 --> 14:51.258
<i>Backdraft-- you
finally watched it?</i>

14:51.293 --> 14:52.659
Yeah.
Wasn't it great?

14:52.694 --> 14:53.827
I thought it was stupid.

14:53.862 --> 14:55.128
Take care, Joe.

15:00.426 --> 15:03.894
You know, tha-that state home we
left Joe in didn't seem so bad.

15:03.929 --> 15:05.095
Yeah, it's got
to be good.

15:05.131 --> 15:06.964
I mean, Napoleon Bonaparte
was there.

15:06.999 --> 15:08.999
Would the French people
let their boss walk around

15:09.035 --> 15:10.675
in stained underwear
trying to stab people

15:10.703 --> 15:12.536
if the place wasn't nice?

15:12.571 --> 15:13.971
Yeah, no, no,
y-you're right, you're right.

15:14.006 --> 15:15.272
Joe will get
much better care there.

15:15.307 --> 15:17.041
I still feel bad.

15:17.076 --> 15:18.809
Come on, you guys.
Joe's gonna be fine.

15:18.844 --> 15:20.044
He'll fit in great there.

15:20.079 --> 15:22.179
Not like when
I went to Hogwarts.

15:22.214 --> 15:24.415
Slytherin.

15:26.118 --> 15:28.118
Hufflepuff.

15:29.822 --> 15:32.890
Housing for registered
sex offenders!

15:32.925 --> 15:35.092
Aw.

15:41.767 --> 15:43.200
Oh, Tori, thank God.

15:43.235 --> 15:44.334
Listen, you got
to unchain me.

15:44.370 --> 15:45.569
Look what Vic did.

15:45.604 --> 15:46.604
Tell me about it.

15:46.639 --> 15:48.238
He's lost his mind.

15:48.274 --> 15:50.307
That's why I'm gonna go stay
with my mother in Baltimore

15:50.342 --> 15:51.842
and work at her wife's bar.

15:51.877 --> 15:53.277
Wait, what?!

15:53.312 --> 15:54.578
Tori, come back!

15:54.613 --> 15:55.646
Damn it!

15:55.681 --> 15:57.247
Wow, shocker.

15:57.283 --> 15:59.616
Your gross hookup
from the car wash ended poorly?

15:59.652 --> 16:00.684
Stewie, thank God!

16:00.720 --> 16:01.785
How'd you find me?

16:01.821 --> 16:03.287
Well, you remember
when the vet knocked you out

16:03.322 --> 16:04.922
to take out that rotten tooth?

16:04.957 --> 16:06.690
He also put a tracking chip
in your neck.

16:06.726 --> 16:08.959
What?! That's a total
violation of my rights!

16:08.994 --> 16:11.328
Heh, I like how you're
chained up in a yard

16:11.363 --> 16:13.063
and still trying
to pretend you're a guy.

16:13.099 --> 16:14.732
Look, you got to help me.

16:14.767 --> 16:16.700
Her husband's a maniac and the
only reason he hasn't killed me

16:16.736 --> 16:18.376
is because he thinks
I'm just his pet dog.

16:18.404 --> 16:20.671
Hmm, he's got
a padlock on here.

16:20.706 --> 16:22.339
But don't worry,
I'll figure something out.

16:22.374 --> 16:25.075
Well, hurry, 'cause I'm trapped
like a baseball announcer.

16:25.111 --> 16:26.810
And the count is two and two.

16:26.846 --> 16:29.279
Garcia steps
off the mound again,

16:29.315 --> 16:31.048
virtually guaranteeing
that my wife

16:31.083 --> 16:32.816
will be asleep when I get home.

16:32.852 --> 16:35.319
The big right-hander kicks
a little dirt and tosses

16:35.354 --> 16:37.888
the rosin bag as my children
grow up without me.

16:37.923 --> 16:40.157
Okay, and now a fan in the
stands is giving me the finger.

16:40.192 --> 16:41.458
I agree.

16:41.494 --> 16:42.760
Hey, I don't know
if you can hear it,

16:42.795 --> 16:45.529
but I'm peeing
in my coffee cup right now.

16:49.702 --> 16:50.702
There you are.

16:50.736 --> 16:52.169
Where the hell have you been?

16:52.204 --> 16:54.772
I got arrested for huckin'
a TV/VCR combo off the dam.

16:54.807 --> 16:56.740
Off the damn what?

16:56.776 --> 16:58.108
Off the damn overpass.

16:58.144 --> 16:59.777
Oh...

16:59.812 --> 17:00.844
God, I love you, Lois.

17:00.880 --> 17:02.346
That was like great sex.

17:02.381 --> 17:04.081
But seriously,
it-it was bad.

17:04.116 --> 17:05.215
It hit a school bus.

17:05.251 --> 17:06.450
Oh, my God!

17:06.485 --> 17:08.085
Well-well, can you
go talk to Joe?

17:08.120 --> 17:10.621
Maybe he can put in a word for
you down at the police station.

17:10.656 --> 17:13.590
Yeah, yeah, Joe, yeah, may--
yeah, maybe, maybe.

17:13.626 --> 17:15.626
Do you, uh, you-you
want a back rub?

17:15.661 --> 17:17.594
Peter, what's going on?

17:17.630 --> 17:19.062
Uh, what do you mean?

17:19.098 --> 17:20.631
Whenever you offer
me a back rub,

17:20.666 --> 17:22.566
it means you're
hiding something.

17:29.141 --> 17:31.175
You, uh, you-you
want a back rub?

17:31.210 --> 17:34.011
We may or may not
have put Joe

17:34.046 --> 17:36.146
in a smelly home
for the goofy.

17:36.182 --> 17:38.916
What?! Peter, those places
are a horror show!

17:38.951 --> 17:40.083
Joe's your friend!

17:40.119 --> 17:41.652
How could you treat
him like that?

17:41.687 --> 17:43.554
We just couldn't handle him
being fully paralyzed.

17:43.589 --> 17:45.189
We didn't know what else to do.

17:45.224 --> 17:46.490
But you're right.

17:46.525 --> 17:48.025
We got to get him out of there.

17:48.060 --> 17:49.660
You most certainly do.

17:49.695 --> 17:51.795
All right, how about
that back rub now?

17:51.831 --> 17:54.198
What are you, nuts?

17:58.237 --> 18:00.304
What the hell do you want?

18:00.339 --> 18:01.605
Oh, hello, sir.

18:01.640 --> 18:03.273
I'm afraid there's
been a mistake.

18:03.309 --> 18:06.977
I believe you found our dog,
and we need to take him home.

18:07.012 --> 18:08.445
No way!
Get lost, kid.

18:08.480 --> 18:10.080
He's my dog now.

18:10.115 --> 18:12.216
Well, we figured
you'd say no to us,

18:12.251 --> 18:14.885
but not to Vice President
Joe Biden!

18:14.920 --> 18:16.453
Oh, my God!

18:16.488 --> 18:17.754
Mr. Vice President!

18:17.790 --> 18:19.423
First, I want
to thank you, Vic,

18:19.458 --> 18:22.359
for shooting the guy
we said was Osama bin Laden.

18:22.394 --> 18:25.162
Second, give these kids
their dog back.

18:25.197 --> 18:27.931
Of course, sir,
I'm so sorry!

18:27.967 --> 18:29.366
Here, take him!

18:29.401 --> 18:30.701
Thank you.

18:30.736 --> 18:32.603
You're a great American.

18:32.638 --> 18:34.004
Thanks, Mr. Biden!

18:34.039 --> 18:35.272
No problem.

18:35.307 --> 18:36.940
<i>Hey, you guys watch Veep?</i>

18:36.976 --> 18:37.941
No.

18:37.977 --> 18:39.409
Yeah, it's all fake.

18:39.445 --> 18:41.245
Yeah, we said no.

18:46.085 --> 18:48.085
Hi, uh, we're here
to pick up Joe Swanson.

18:48.120 --> 18:49.386
Are you from the news?

18:49.421 --> 18:51.054
You have to tell us
if you're from the news.

18:51.090 --> 18:52.789
No, we're his friends.

18:52.825 --> 18:54.057
What are you guys
doing here?

18:54.093 --> 18:55.359
We came to bring
you home, Joe.

18:55.394 --> 18:57.928
We're all really sorry
we abandoned you.

18:57.963 --> 19:00.864
Yeah, we just kind of got
overwhelmed and all freaked out.

19:00.900 --> 19:02.666
But we're your
friends, Joe.

19:02.701 --> 19:04.935
And we'll always be there
for you no matter what.

19:04.970 --> 19:06.503
Thanks, guys.

19:06.538 --> 19:09.206
I'd say let's get my stuff,
but it's all been stolen.

19:09.241 --> 19:10.207
That's okay.

19:10.242 --> 19:12.009
Come on, let's go home.

19:12.044 --> 19:13.477
Sorry, no one
gets out of here

19:13.512 --> 19:15.178
without a release
from their doctor.

19:15.214 --> 19:18.415
All right, we'll just
call him right now.

19:22.221 --> 19:24.221
What's that ringing?

19:27.793 --> 19:30.360
Joe, that ringing--
it's coming from your back!

19:30.396 --> 19:31.495
It is?

19:31.530 --> 19:32.896
Holy crap!

19:32.932 --> 19:35.032
Dr. Hartman must have
dropped his phone in Joe

19:35.067 --> 19:36.466
when he was looking
at his spine!

19:36.502 --> 19:37.601
Oh, thank God.

19:37.636 --> 19:39.503
I've been hearing
that ringing all week.

19:39.538 --> 19:40.971
I just thought
I was losing my mind

19:41.006 --> 19:43.407
from lunatics
screaming in my face.

19:43.442 --> 19:45.542
Your mother's a whore!

19:45.577 --> 19:48.946
I told you that
in confidence, Gary.

19:52.985 --> 19:54.985
Ah, it's so great
to have you back, Joe.

19:55.020 --> 19:56.553
You seem good as new.

19:56.588 --> 19:58.488
Yeah, it turns out Dr.
Hartman's cell phone

19:58.524 --> 20:00.424
was pressing on
my spinal cord,

20:00.459 --> 20:03.126
and that's what was causing
my total paralysis.

20:03.162 --> 20:05.262
Yeah, sorry we dropped
the ball for a while,

20:05.297 --> 20:07.831
which is the way we agreed we'd
describe what we did to you,

20:07.866 --> 20:09.599
which hopefully
makes it seem less heinous.

20:09.635 --> 20:11.001
It's all right, guys.

20:11.036 --> 20:12.803
I'm just glad to be
back on my feet.

20:12.838 --> 20:15.539
Well, you know
what I mean.

20:18.210 --> 20:21.011
<i>I never saw much
of Joe after that.</i>

20:21.046 --> 20:22.713
<i>And while he's been gone
for many years,</i>

20:22.748 --> 20:24.614
<i>I've never forgotten his face</i>

20:24.650 --> 20:27.117
<i>or his laughter.</i>

20:28.520 --> 20:30.454
Come on, are we
going to the beach?

20:30.489 --> 20:32.089
We've been waiting forever.

20:32.124 --> 20:33.657
Yeah, be right there,
champ.

20:33.692 --> 20:36.059
He said that the first
two times we asked.

20:36.095 --> 20:40.630
I know, he spaces out
when he's at the computer.

20:48.640 --> 20:50.307
<i>These aren't my kids.</i>

20:50.342 --> 20:51.908
<i>And also, this isn't
play wrestling.</i>

20:51.944 --> 20:53.410
<i>We're actually fighting.</i>

20:57.299 --> 21:03.799
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru